problems.solution:
**A model answer.** `tests/practice-checker.spec.ts`:

```ts
import { test } from '@playwright/test';
import { fillRegistrationForm, expectFormFilled } from './registration-helpers';

test('the checker notices a wrong email', async ({ page }) => {
  await fillRegistrationForm(page, 'ada@example.com');
  await expectFormFilled(page, 'ada@example.com');
});
```

Run it with `npx playwright test tests/practice-checker.spec.ts --project=chromium`:

```output
Running 1 test using 1 worker
  1 passed (4.2s)
```

With `expectFormFilled(page, 'wrong@example.com')` on the last line, the same command reports `1 failed`, and the error contains these two lines:

```output
    Expected: "wrong@example.com"
    Received: "ada@example.com"
```

**What to check in your own answer.** The error names `registration-helpers.ts:21`, because the assertion that failed is the first line of `expectFormFilled`. Below it, the error names `practice-checker.spec.ts:6`, which is the line of the test that called the helper. The `Received` line shows the email that `fillRegistrationForm` typed, so the page was right and the expected value was wrong.
